# Ratchet for warning-level findings from `verikt check` on this repository.
#
# These are real findings, not false positives: functions over the 50-line limit in
# code-quality.md, plus advisory anti-patterns. Generated code is excluded via
# check.exclude in verikt.yaml, so everything counted here is hand-written. They do not
# fail the build, because only error severity does — but without a ceiling they accumulate
# unnoticed, and "warnings we live with" quietly becomes the baseline.
#
# `mise run verify` fails if the count rises above this number (GitHub Actions does
# not run for this repository, so that local gate is the only enforcement). Lower it when you pay
# debt down; raising it should be a deliberate, reviewed decision with a reason in the
# commit message.
#
# Measure with a freshly embedded engine — `mise run verify` does this — or the number
# reflects whatever engine your binary happens to carry rather than the one CI builds.
# A figure of 69 recorded earlier was measured against a stale engine and was four short.
#
# 69 -> 68: max_lines counted one of the two brace rows as a line of code, so a function
# with exactly 50 lines in its body was reported as 51 and flagged. One function here was
# in that position. The finding was false, not paid down.
#
# 68 -> 46: global_mutable_state reported unexported lookup tables that nothing writes to.
# Go has no const map or slice, so those vars are the only way to express a table, and 21
# of the 22 findings were false. Also false, also not paid down — see
# internal/engineclient/testdata/detector-restraint, which now fails the build if a
# detector fires on code a careful engineer would write.
#
# 46 -> 44: paid down. ValidateVeriktYAML (validateSeverityOverrides) and
# split.go's index builder came under 50 lines while porting #13 and #15;
# checkWithEngineOnly, DefaultVeriktConfig and newCheckCommand were kept
# under the limit as they grew.
#
# 44 -> 40: paid down. Porting #21 and #23 brought renderFilesDir,
# RenderCapabilityFiles, PreviewCapabilityFiles, RenderComposition and the check
# verdict logic under the limits.
#
# 40 -> 39: paid down. runGuide came under the limit when the --catalog-only
# path moved into runGuideCatalogOnly, fixing the #36 review findings.
39
